course: dictionary
lesson: 6157
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Mimosa can mean a tree with fluffy flowers, a small plant whose leaves fold when you touch them, or a drink. The words around the word tell you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «The sensitive plant, mimosa, folds its leaflets within seconds when touched.» The folding and the touching tell you this is the small plant, not the tree or the drink. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Try each meaning in the sentence, one at a time, and keep the one that makes sense. If a meaning makes the sentence silly, it is the wrong one.
fact: Mimosa has several meanings, so check the context to find which one is meant.
fact: A mimosa can be a tree or shrub with fluffy yellow or pink flowers.
fact: The sensitive plant is a small plant whose leaves fold up when you touch them.
fact: «The sensitive plant, mimosa, folds its leaflets within seconds when touched» because water moves out of cells at the base of each leaf.
fact: A mimosa drink is orange juice and sparkling wine, and it is for adults. In the UK it is called a Buck's Fizz.
exercise: «The sensitive plant, mimosa, folds its leaflets within seconds when touched.» Which meaning of mimosa is this? | A tree with fluffy yellow flowers | A drink of orange juice and sparkling wine | *A small plant whose leaves fold up when touched | A bright pink fruit
exercise: In France, mimosa flowers mark early spring. What is the mimosa here? | A plant whose leaves fold up | A drink for adults | *A tree or shrub with fluffy yellow or pink flowers | A kind of sweet cake
exercise: Ella says a mimosa is a drink for children. What is wrong with her idea? | The drink is made of milk and cocoa | The drink is called a Buck's Fizz only in France | *The drink is for adults | Nothing, she is right
test: Which clue in «The sensitive plant, mimosa, folds its leaflets within seconds when touched» shows the meaning? | The word plant only | The word sensitive, and folds when touched | The word leaflets, which means a sweet | *Folds when touched, which is what the small plant does
test: A child asks for a mimosa at a party. Why should an adult check first? | Because mimosa flowers only bloom in winter | *Because the mimosa drink is for adults | Because the sensitive plant bites | Because the mimosa tree is poisonous to touch
exam: Which meaning fits «mimosa plants dropped again and again without harm stopped folding»? | A drink of orange juice and sparkling wine | *A small sensitive plant whose leaves fold up | A tree with fluffy yellow flowers | A fruit that grows in France
